3. **Transformation rule summary**:  
   - Find the largest contiguous rectangular block of non-background colors that is not monochrome (i.e., contains at least two colors) and is fully filled (no background inside). This is the “pattern”.  
   - Identify all other non-background pixels that are not part of this pattern. Compute the bounding box of these pixels.  
   - Create a binary mask within this bounding box: 1 if the corresponding cell (relative to bounding box top-left) contains any of those other non-background pixels, else 0.  
   - Output grid dimensions: (pattern height × bounding box height) rows, (pattern width × bounding box width) columns.  
   - For each cell (i,j) in the bounding box grid (i from 0 to bounding box height-1, j from 0 to bounding box width-1), if mask[i][j] == 1, copy the pattern to output block starting at row i*pattern_height, column j*pattern_width. Else, fill that block with the background color (the most common color in input, usually the one surrounding the pattern).  

