   - Identify room colors: all other non-zero colors (excluding 0 and D). Each room color R must have at least one connected component with more than, say, 3 cells.

   - For each room color R, compute n = the number of cells of color R that are orthogonally adjacent to at least one cell of color D.

   - For each R, create a row of length 4 consisting of R repeated (4 - n) times, followed by D repeated n times.

   - Sort the rows first by n descending, then by R ascending (numerical order).

   - The output grid is the list of these rows.

